Changes to rtd266x_programmer (https://github.com/bleughb/rtd266x_programmer, commit e83f32e)
SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0 (these changes only; the tool itself is not part of this repository)

Apply in a clone of the tool:   patch -p1 < rtd266x_programmer.patch   then   make

- Chip entries: MX25L4005 (512 KB, the size was wrong in some copies), MX25L2005 (256 KB),
  Puya P25Q40H, Zbit ZB25VQ40 (JEDEC 0x5E6013); Macronix, Puya and Zbit use the
  same command codes as Winbond.
- i2clinux.cpp: include <linux/i2c-dev.h> directly (builds on current Linux).
- Status register writes wait for the chip to finish and are retried.
- Refuses to erase while the flash is still write protected, and says why.
- Waits for the chip erase to finish before writing.
- Prints "Flash OK" / "FLASH FAILED" from the CRC check (it was printed but not judged).
- -w <reg> (experimental): drive the flash WP# pin through an MCU register
  (ThinkVision LT1913p: 0xd7). Unlocks the status register there, but writing still fails.
- -t <addr>: safe write test in an empty, unused 4 KB sector.

